{"id": "en_story_hudson", "tag": "AVIATION", "cta": "MORE TRUE STORIES LIKE THIS", "ctaSmall": "follow", "ctaWhere": "new story every day", "accent": "#4FC3F7", "lang": "en", "total": 69.83, "segments": [{"text": "On 15 January 2009, US Airways Flight 1549 departs from LaGuardia airport into the cold morning sky.", "start": 0.0, "end": 6.58}, {"text": "The Airbus A320 climbs steadily until it hits a dense flock of Canada geese at about 2,800 feet.", "start": 7.12, "end": 12.32}, {"text": "Both engines instantly ingest the birds and completely lose all thrust over the busy New York area.", "start": 12.78, "end": 17.1}, {"text": "Captain Chesley Sully Sullenberger and first officer Jeffrey Skiles face a nightmare scenario in the cockpit.", "start": 17.56, "end": 22.0}, {"text": "Less than four minutes pass from the initial bird strike to the final terrifying moments of flight.", "start": 22.54, "end": 26.26}, {"text": "The experienced crew quickly realizes they do not have enough altitude to reach any nearby airport safely.", "start": 26.62, "end": 30.78}, {"text": "Every single second counts as the massive commercial airplane descends rapidly toward the frozen city below.", "start": 31.22, "end": 35.34}, {"text": "Captain Sully makes the split second decision to aim the powerless aircraft toward the Hudson River.", "start": 35.86, "end": 39.4}, {"text": "Passengers brace for impact as the metal hull glides silently down toward the water near Midtown Manhattan.", "start": 39.94, "end": 43.76}, {"text": "The skilled pilots execute a textbook ditching that shocks experts watching from the skyscrapers above them.", "start": 44.3, "end": 48.3}, {"text": "Frigid water surrounds the floating fuselage immediately after the violent impact shakes the cabin doors open.", "start": 48.76, "end": 52.96}, {"text": "Rescue boats and NY Waterway ferries arrive within minutes to pluck freezing survivors from the surface.", "start": 53.52, "end": 57.3}, {"text": "Miraculously, all 155 